== Overview ==
The '''Quad Rocket Mutant Toilet''' appears on Wave 49 of [[Nightmare Mode|Nightmare Mode.]] It currently has 1.64M HP. It moves slowly but will stun units very fast. (It uses his 4 rockets and 2 lasers to stun the units). It got demoted to wave 49 because of [[Scientist Toilet]].
== Waves ==
=== Nightmare Mode: ===
Wave 49: 1,640,000 HP x1
=== Nightmare Mode Old: ===
Wave 50: 1,670,000 HP x1
== Strategy ==
* The [[Quad Rocket Mutant Toilet]] is an extremely strong enemy, as it is one of the final bosses of [[Nightmare Mode|Nightmare Mode.]] High DPS [[units]] are required to defeat this [[Enemies|enemy]] as it has a high amount of health, being 1,640,000 HP.
* It also stuns units very frequently with its 4 rockets, so [[Medic Cameraman]] or [[Camera Repair Drone]] is required to unstun units, or you will not do enough DPS to take this enemy down as your DPS units will be stunned. 
* It can be slowed by Level 5/6 [[Upgraded Titan Cameraman]], [[TV Woman|TV Woman,]] or [[Mech Cameraman|Mech Cameraman,]] making it slightly easier to take down.
* [[Upgraded Titan Cameraman]] not only has a high amount of DPS but will also slow down this enemy with its core flames.
* [[Upgraded Titan Speakerman]] can absorb stuns that are from the [[Quad Rocket Mutant Toilet]], making it easier for [[Medic Cameraman]] or [[Camera Repair Drone]].

== Trivia ==
* It is based on the [https://skibidi-toilet.fandom.com/wiki/Dual_Laser_Launcher_Skibidi_Toilet?so=search Dual Laser Launcher Skibidi Toilet] from the series. It is recommended to defeat this toilet with the highest DPS in the game like Mythics.
* When it was first released in the [[Episode 59 Update]], it was the final boss, it was moved down to wave 49 when the [[Scientist Toilet]] released.
* It will most likely be moved down to wave 48 if there is a new final boss.
* It has a special animation when it shoots rockets.

